WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:06.259
In the last few weeks I've gotten requests
on doing videos on entrepreneurship having

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:11.000
to do with family, how to run a business with
family, what it means to be married to an

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.440
entrepreneur, how is an entrepreneur supposed
to be before you date someone who's an entrepreneur.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.630
All of these things that I've put together
because you requested them and today I decided

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.880
to do an episode dedicated to mothers.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:28.000
Why I believe most mothers would make very
good entrepreneurs.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.019
This is from pure experience.

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:31.199
I've mentored a lot of different people.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:36.640
I've mentored single fathers, single mothers,
husbands and wives, ladies by themselves,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.750
mothers by themselves, and I can see certain
strengths mothers have that helps them in

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:41.750
their business.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:47.741
You've got to always know and lead with the
strengths that you have in business, and I

00:00:47.741 --> 00:00:52.580
think these are the strengths that mothers
have that you need to tap into this to help

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:56.140
and leverage your business to grow even faster
and excel.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.920
Let me get right into it.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.900
I came up with 14 of them -- I'm sure there's
more, but I came up with 14 of them that I

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.580
feel are particular to moms.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.170
So let's start off with the first one.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.649
They tend to deliver bad news gently.

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:16.740
There's something about the way a mother delivers
bad news.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.369
They're a little more tender about it.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:22.100
They're a little bit more understanding about
it.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.280
They are more concerned about the other person's
feelings on when they want to tell them "here's

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.869
what happened, here's what happened, here's
what happened," where the other person's taking

00:01:29.869 --> 00:01:33.869
it better vs. a father may say, "It doesn't
matter.

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:34.869
. . here's what you need to do.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:35.869
" And it's boom.

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:37.969
And the kid goes in his room.

00:01:37.969 --> 00:01:39.689
They have some feelings as well.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:42.170
Mothers are better at dealing with that than
fathers.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:45.170
That's a strength of yours when it comes to
dealing with business.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.359
Second, they have natural leadership instincts.

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:52.630
I think mothers have a very sixth sense.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.290
They know things that are going on that maybe
nobody else knows what's going on.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.479
They have leadership instincts.

00:01:57.479 --> 00:01:58.479
They can feel.

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:05.759
One of the reasons they have such an edge
is that mothers tend to spend more time with

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:11.319
kids then fathers do and when you spend more
time with kids -- this is not in all cases

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:18.450
-- but when you spend more time with kids,
kids are all emotional.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:25.140
So your sensitivity toward emotion goes even
higher than a man would or a father would

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.920
because you're around it more.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:27.920
Kids are very good teachers.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.800
So can you imagine if kids are very good teachers,
mothers are getting more teaching from kids

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.410
than fathers are because kids teach us about
emotions and feelings.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:43.170
So your natural ability to be able to read
people is much better.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.050
This is why a lot of times a mother says,
"I don't get a good feeling about that person

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.080
or I don't get a good feeling about this."

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.550
They have a certain intuition because they
see it with their kids all the time.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.110
So you have natural leadership instinct.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:07.960
Point number three would be, you're not afraid
to speak your mind.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:13.070
I think mothers will approach problems and
say, "Son, I don't like how you're handling

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.070
this."

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.000
"Honey, I don't like how this is taking place.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.240
I don't like the way we did this.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.720
I don't know if we're doing the right thing
here."

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.310
Mothers will generally say this.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.650
Fathers may set aside the problems and just
go and say, "I'll figure it out."

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.720
Mothers will bring it up.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.980
They're naturally not afraid to speak their
mind.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:36.130
In business, it helps you a lot to talk about
the things that are taking place in business

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:40.800
and it helps resolve issues sooner rather
than delaying an issue that's going to take

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.120
place that we have to resolve 7 months from
now.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.490
Mothers do it now.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:56.340
Next, typically, and this is kind of a strange
way of describing it, (men, we can learn a

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:03.490
lot from this), but mothers typically have
other mothers that they confide in and they

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:04.530
talk about their problems.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:13.330
So they have natural mentors, other people
that they talk to that are in the same situation

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.330
as them.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:22.650
This allows them to release a certain frustration
that they're having as a mother raising her

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.310
kids, as you see someone else who is going
through it as well.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:32.400
So if you use that same ability and find other
entrepreneurs to confide in who are in a similar

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:38.440
situation as you, to understand you, and those
who overcome -- not those that necessarily

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.290
want to say, "this is why we can't run a business."

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:41.350
I'm not talking about that.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.090
Just because you're a mother, doesn't make
you a great entrepreneur.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.630
Let's get that part open.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.600
I'm not trying to be diplomatic here.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.040
I'm just telling you that just because someone's
a mother doesn't mean she'll make a great

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.040
entrepreneur.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.440
There are still negative and positive mothers.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.240
I'm talking about somebody who is positive,
that is truly wanting to build a business.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.780
If you tap into that same ability to confide
in your peers to find that the situation there

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:08.070
and you do the same in business and find a
mentor, you'll generally find a way to solve

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.960
that problem or overcome that issue that you're
addressing at that time.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.630
Next is urgency.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.630
Entrepreneurs are urgent.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.190
The reason they're urgent is because they
have so many things going on -- drop off the

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:22.480
kids, pick up the food, boom, job, school,
music.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.139
. . You have so many things -- here's what
I've got.

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:29.190
10 minutes, 15 minute call, there's a certain
level of urgency when you're dealing with

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.960
mothers because there's only 24 hours in a
day and there's so many things that need to

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:33.960
get done.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:39.580
Somehow, some way, they tend to get more things
done, mothers do, as entrepreneurs.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.450
The next thing is natural networking skills.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:47.340
I would say moms are very good at asking,
"Who do you know that does this, who do you

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.400
know that does that, who do you know this.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.460
. .?" Men, we tend to kind of think we know
it all, we tend to think we don't need help,

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:58.300
so networking wise, they don't mind asking
anybody who they know in this area, so they're

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.639
very good when it comes to asking for referrals.

00:06:01.639 --> 00:06:07.830
My gosh, I've had sales people in our company,
54% of the agents in our company are ladies.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:13.360
And those who are some of the best producers
in our company are mothers who are very good

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.270
at working the referral market.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.610
And the referral market is "who do you know?"

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:22.550
And that comes from natural networking skills
that you already have in place to use and

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:23.550
apply.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:26.540
Remember, a lot of these things I may be saying
right now, and you're a mother watching this

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.120
and you're saying, "How come I don't use that
skill?"

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.389
You've got to use it for it to work!

00:06:31.389 --> 00:06:34.701
You have the muscle -- it's almost like you
have that weapon in your arsenal, and if you're

00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:38.410
not using it in business, it won't do anything
for you.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.540
You have to take these things and actually
apply them and you'll realize how simple it

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:46.480
is because you've been doing it all your life
already.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:50.670
Point #7 is there's a certain level of trustworthiness,
for mothers.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.670
There's a certain level of trust.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.510
I don't know how to describe this.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.480
You know, if someone is selling me something
and they're a mother and they have kids, I

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:01.100
can tell you myself as a buyer, I trust.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:05.479
Because for me, I always think a mother is
going to give the right feedback because she

00:07:05.479 --> 00:07:10.479
has a kid and she knows she doesn't want anyone
to take advantage of her kids so probably

00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:12.610
she's not going to want to take advantage
of me.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:19.040
So in my mind, as a person, I trust a mother's
selling in the area of business when it comes

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.389
down to wanting to buy their product.

00:07:21.389 --> 00:07:23.690
The next one is emotions.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.370
Tenderhearted.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:31.340
It goes back to when I told you they deliver
bad news better, but this is more about the

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:32.340
listening side.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.840
When I say emotions, they make better listeners.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:39.750
So if a client wants to buy something, and
let's just say they sit there and say, "Well,

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.430
you know, let me tell you my experience with
the last person."

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.430
"Tell me about it."

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:46.370
Well, the last person I dealt with, he did
this, he did this, he did this, he did that."

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.300
"How did that make you feel?"

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.300
"It made me feel this way."

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.300
"What do you think about that?

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.300
What do you think about that John?

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.050
What do you think about that Mary?

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:57.009
What are some things you'd want to be different
when you do business with somebody new?"

00:07:57.009 --> 00:08:03.050
They're very good at displaying listening
skills, to hearing you out.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:07.760
Men just want to give the next big positive,
popular answer to be impressive and say, "Did

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.760
you hear that comeback I gave?!"

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.430
Sometimes we forget, we don't even know that.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:18.020
But mothers are very good at saying, "Okay,
I'm hearing you out" and we like to be heard

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:22.810
out, and as a customer we want to talk to
somebody that's listening to our issues and

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:26.570
our challenges, and hopefully they'll figure
out a way to resolve it, if we trust.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:30.410
Which in a sense like this, we would because
we're dealing with a mother that's got a higher

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.099
trusting rate than the rest.

00:08:33.099 --> 00:08:34.820
Next, they ask a lot of questions.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.550
Point #9, you know, when a kid comes home
from school.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.550
. . practice again.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.010
When they're picked up, "How was school?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.010
What did you learn today?

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.010
What did that guy say?

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:43.010
What did that girl say?

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.010
What's that girl's name?

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.010
What does that girl do?

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:46.010
Who's your best friend?

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:49.740
Are you hanging out with that guy?" They want
to know everything, right?

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:50.740
Think about it!

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:54.500
Oh my God, my mom asked me all the questions
on the drive home, and I know what she's trying

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.500
to ask me.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.150
They're trying to figure out clues, right?

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:59.290
So why is she hanging out?

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.140
When I picked her up, she was talking to this
guy.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.740
"So tell me about that guy.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.230
I like your friend."

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.960
She was talking to that other guy and that
other guy's a senior and her daughter's a

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:08.960
freshman.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.010
"I noticed you were talking.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.200
Is that the football player?

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.410
Is he the quarterback?

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.410
Good looking guy.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.410
Tell me about him.

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.480
How many times have you guys hung out?"

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:18.950
Mom's trying to find out if there's anything
going on with that quarterback and the daughter.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.910
It's the same exact thing in sales or in business.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:27.270
A mother asks questions to get to the issue
of resolving to see if this may be a problem

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:31.060
that they have to overcome later on when it
comes to asking for a check or asking for

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.060
the sale.

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:36.160
I'm going to resolve this right now is what
I need to do when it comes to asking questions.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.301
No matter what happens -- office situations,
environment, leadership, it all comes down

00:09:40.301 --> 00:09:42.710
to the questions you're asking the people
you're dealing with.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:48.190
So mothers, because they ask very good questions,
they also make very, very good negotiators.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:51.250
Point #10: They make very, very good negotiators.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.950
They negotiate with their kids, they negotiate
with their husbands, they have to get the

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:58.210
husbands to be willing to pay for something,
they have to be getting the families to settle

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.800
and come together, they have to be willing
to put a birthday party where the in-laws

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:04.300
don't want to get together with the other
in-laws and there's negotiation going on with

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:08.020
the in-laws and she's in the middle trying
to get both parties to work -- there's so

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:13.800
much negotiation going on with mothers that
-- there's a lot of skills that you have that

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:19.410
there's not a price tag to put on there because
you didn't go to university to learn it for

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:20.410
$200,000.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:22.720
It's the life university that mothers go through.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.650
But you've got to use those skills.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:28.350
You've got to use those skills for business
to see the results.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.830
Point #11: They are superior multi-taskers.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:36.530
There's not a debate here to say whether multi-tasking
is real or not.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.530
I've done a video on that.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.040
If you want to debate that, go watch that
video.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:41.839
Mothers are better multi-taskers.

00:10:41.839 --> 00:10:45.870
They hold the baby, they cook, and they talk
to the husband simultaneously.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.520
Three actions going on at the same time.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.700
They are better multi-taskers.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.760
And sometimes in business, you're going to
be doing multi-tasking.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:56.020
#12: Better problem solvers.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.709
They solve problems very well.

00:10:57.709 --> 00:11:01.170
Again, the practice they get on solving problems
on who?

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.170
Kids!

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:06.339
It's constant problems that they're facing
with kids, so they have to become better problem

00:11:06.339 --> 00:11:10.030
solvers because they're getting practice non-stop
with their kids already.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:12.180
#13: Tolerance for pain.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:19.010
I had to write this down because my wife's
had two kids and she has one on the way and

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:25.810
I've been part of both of those deliveries
and I see some of the things mothers go through.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:29.540
Your tolerance for pain is unreal.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.720
There's a reason why you were chosen to be
a mother, a woman.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:38.640
If you have a child, there's a reason you
are where you are with that.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.410
You've got to know there's a reason for that.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:46.600
Your tolerance for pain, when it comes to
business -- I once heard a lady who owned

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.029
a business and raised kids.

00:11:48.029 --> 00:11:51.709
And she started a startup, and she lost a
couple of startups and one of them worked.

00:11:51.709 --> 00:11:57.730
She said, "The closest thing a man will ever
experience to giving birth to a baby is starting

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.020
a new company."

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:03.899
And I sat there and said, "That's pretty interesting
because it's painful to start a business sometimes,

00:12:03.899 --> 00:12:07.470
because you're going through having to learn
so much all at the same time, but because

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:11.262
mothers have a tolerance for pain, they're
able to channel that into business and they

00:12:11.262 --> 00:12:15.240
can leverage that, and use it as an upper
hand for themselves.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:19.310
Point # 14 is event planning.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:27.500
You're generally better event planners -- weddings,
birthdays, you have so much practice doing

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:32.730
that, that when it comes down to business
events, putting events together, for business,

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.850
you have an upper hand, you have a very big
upper hand, and in business it's all about

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:42.149
putting nice events together, networking,
taking care of people, hosting good events.

00:12:42.149 --> 00:12:49.019
When you put good events with charities and
whether it's profit or cigar or wine or parties

00:12:49.019 --> 00:12:53.060
-- all these types of things, this is when
people come and ask, "who hosted this event?"Such

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.209
and such did.

00:12:54.209 --> 00:12:55.280
She put the event together?

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:56.860
Then everyone goes to her as a referral.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:13:02.360
You're a better event planner in business
and that helps you out a lot when it comes

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.470
to the business side.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:07.870
Lastly, mothers tend to unite people.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.490
Mothers bring kids together.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.430
Mothers tend to bring families together.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.899
Mothers tend to keep the siblings together.

00:13:13.899 --> 00:13:16.980
Mothers tend to keep the son and the father
close together.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:23.950
Mothers tend to -- when one of the kids is
going through issues, relationships with their

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.980
spouse, they tend to want to keep them together.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.850
They have a strength of unity and uniting
people.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:33.100
That helps you in business because in business,
say a vendor and you don't get along.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:37.031
They can bring you together and figure out
a way to say, "What are you not happy about?

00:13:37.031 --> 00:13:38.209
What is the number you want?

00:13:38.209 --> 00:13:39.209
We can't pay over this.

00:13:39.209 --> 00:13:40.209
What can we do about this?

00:13:40.209 --> 00:13:41.209
Can we make this work?

00:13:41.209 --> 00:13:43.800
We like you, you like us, we've been together
for awhile, why don't we just try to make

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:44.800
this work?

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.000
Great, you want our business, right?

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.000
Yes, we want your business.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.120
We've been together for 11 years.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.910
Do we really want to make this relationship
be sour over one simple sale that we don't

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:52.910
agree over $1,000?

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:53.910
No.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.100
Why don't we make it work?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.100
So unite.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.100
There's a strength in doing that.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.470
So you got 15 things.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.269
Now there's a lot more, and I'd love to hear
from you if you want to post it on the bottom

00:14:01.269 --> 00:14:03.680
and comment and let us know what I've missed
here.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:05.430
But I can tell you one thing here.

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:09.240
If you watch this and you're not a mother,
but you know other people who are entrepreneurs

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.050
and they're mothers, share this video with
them.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.480
On behalf of Mother's Day, send them a Happy
Mother's Day.

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:21.790
And know that for me, I look for mothers that
I do business with and I see their strengths

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:22.790
in business.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:26.329
They're incredible because they have certain
skill sets that others don't have and I need

00:14:26.329 --> 00:14:30.740
to bring it out in them and show it to them
that they have this ability already.

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:31.950
Let's put it to use.

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:35.860
You've been doing this for the last 9 years
with your three kids, let's put this to use.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:39.740
You've been using these things for the last
17 years, you already know how to do this,

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:41.700
why aren't you doing this in business?

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:42.700
Let's put that to use.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:47.040
So on behalf of all the mothers that also
follow Valuetainment -- and I get lots of

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:51.370
nice messages from you -- and we did a survey
the other day, and I listened to a lot of

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:54.380
the comments that the mothers sent on the
survey that we did.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:58.950
And we definitely want to let you know that
I'm thankful for you as well, and I am who

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:03.279
I am as well because I had a single mother
that raised me at some period as well and

00:15:03.279 --> 00:15:07.399
there's some impact that was made on my life
-- a tremendous impact made on my life.

00:15:07.399 --> 00:15:10.950
And I want to give some love to all the mothers
out there who are entrepreneurs.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:16.029
Go out there and use your strengths to your
advantage so you can succeed as an entrepreneur

00:15:16.029 --> 00:15:17.029
as well.

00:15:17.029 --> 00:15:21.870
And if you haven't subscribed to this channel,
please be sure to do so on the bottom here.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:26.180
If you're watching this video somewhere else,
on a different website, visit patrickbetdavid.com.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:29.720
Thank you.

